Add native VS Code workspace for rumpelpod

Add a workspace extension that switches pods from an Activity Bar view.
Attach agent and shell sessions in sidebar xterm terminals. Show pod
changes in native VS Code multi-diff editors. Run CLI commands under a
packaged node-pty binding. Pod creation, lifecycle output, and
interactive sessions share the CLI's established terminal behavior.

Expose JSON list and review snapshots plus daemon invalidation events.
Use them for live status and review updates. Notify review clients from
a bounded host post-receive hook while preserving user hooks and custom
daemon sockets. Keep this as the only new terminal-related rumpel core
surface. Do not retain the abandoned daemon PTY streaming routes or API.

Publish separate Linux x64, Linux arm64, and macOS arm64 VSIX assets.
Build them in existing platform jobs. Preserve the multi-binary rumpel
tarball and installer. Build Linux bindings in a pinned Bullseye image.
Reject bindings above the supported glibc baseline. Keep normal pipeline
extension checks local so they do not start nested Docker builds.

Provide a loopback-only live code-server workspace backed by a small
anyhow demo repository and lingering user services. Persist only
allowlisted agent credentials for those services. Use the same complete
devcontainer image in development and CI, and report startup logs when
its entrypoint fails. Pin the arm64 code-server archive to its published
digest. Keep the timing-sensitive Playwright test available only through
the explicit ignored-test flag.
